  "summary": "An Ark audit found that 34 outside police agencies ran 8,542 federally entangled searches of Tiburon's Flock license-plate cameras in the first seven months of 2026, despite Tiburon rewriting its ALPR policy in December and requiring monthly audits. More than 4,800 of those searches came after the police chief said external searches were limited to valid reasons, and three organizations appeared not to qualify to receive the data.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Thirty-four outside police agencies ran 8,542 searches of Tiburon's license-plate cameras for federally entangled investigations in the seven months after the town rewrote its plate-reader policy in December and began requiring monthly audits, a new Ark audit has found.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "the town had worked with vendor Flock Safety \"to allow external searches only for valid reasons\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Twenty-six still have access to the cameras, and eight of those ran searches flagged by The Ark as federally entangled as recently as July.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
